                <strong>Station Coverage Is Incomplete for Niche Fuels.</strong> While E10 and B7_STANDARD are reported by the vast majority of the {total_stations:,} stations, niche fuels like {least_covered} ({cov_counts[least_covered]} stations) and HVO ({cov_counts.get('HVO', 0)} stations) have very limited coverage. This limits the scheme's utility for consumers of alternative fuels.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Market Stability Observed.</strong> No significant daily price volatility was detected during February 2026. Prices were broadly stable, suggesting a market in equilibrium over the observation period. This is consistent with a commodity-driven pricing model where retailers respond to wholesale costs that change gradually.
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

</div>

<footer>
    <p>UK Retail Fuel Price Trend Analysis — February 2026 &middot; Data source: UK Government Fuel Finder via fuelcosts.co.uk (CC BY 4.0)</p>
